WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.074 --> 00:00:02.635
-Leslie, you're not afraid
to speak your mind

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.270
and you always give great
advice, so I thought, right now,

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.872
you could help some people
with their big life decisions.

00:00:06.872 --> 00:00:09.275
It's time for
"Life Coach with Leslie Jones."

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:10.677
Here we go.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:15.314
-♪ "Life Coach
with Leslie Jones" ♪

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:16.583
-Ah! Very nice.

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:19.252
So, we asked viewers at home
to send in questions

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:20.820
that they need your coaching on.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.721
You ready to give out
some tough advice?

00:00:22.721 --> 00:00:25.124
-I am so ready.

00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:28.228
-Alright, here we go.
This first question is...

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.476
-Absolutely!
-Really? Wow.

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:47.246
-Now, this is how
you need to handle this.

00:00:47.246 --> 00:00:48.648
You sit them down and go,

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:51.951
"Listen, we've been here before,
the whole family.

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:54.954
We've been here before.
Twice, it didn't work.

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:59.258
So what we're going to do is,
if you make it two months,

00:00:59.258 --> 00:01:00.827
we'll buy you a present."

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:04.730
-[ Laughs ] Yes!

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:06.799
That's exactly right.

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:08.501
Just two months.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:14.406
-Even if the present
is a damn divorce.

00:01:14.406 --> 00:01:15.408
-Just -- We'll get you --

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:16.976
Just two months,
we'll get you a present.

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:20.480
Yeah. This is great.
Alright, here we go.

00:01:31.924 --> 00:01:33.993
-You're not supposed
to be friends

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.095
with your people
that you work with.

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:37.530
That's a work thing.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.466
So she should have never
saw that shirt, sir.

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:43.302
Second answer -- block her ass.

00:01:43.302 --> 00:01:48.040
And then, when she asks you
why you blocked her, said,

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:54.413
"Hey, you have mistaken me
for somebody else, sweetie.

00:01:54.413 --> 00:01:57.950
I have -- You have a husband,
I've got a relationship.

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:00.920
You liked the picture
that I didn't have my shirt on.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.821
I ain't like that."

00:02:02.821 --> 00:02:05.958
-Wow. Alright.
-Y'all gotta get some gumption.

00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:08.528
Start getting some gumption.
Start telling folks.

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:12.098
Stop acting like you're trying
to save somebody's feelings.

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:13.967
They wasn't saving
your feelings.

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:15.668
She wasn't thinking about
your feelings

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:18.671
when she liked the picture.

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:22.408
-Dude, I agree.
Shouldn't have liked it.

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:24.844
Alright, here, how about this?

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:38.958
-Okay, yes, you do,
but you confront him in

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:41.360
a restaurant full of people,

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:45.064
just in case you found out
his secret identity

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:47.766
and he try to choke you out
and kill you and bury you.

00:02:47.766 --> 00:02:49.802
-Choke you out, yeah.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:52.371
-So, that's --
Yeah, do it in public.

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:53.505
-Public place, yep.

00:02:53.505 --> 00:02:55.875
-Don't confront him
while y'all watching TV.

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:58.177
He's going to kill you.

00:02:58.177 --> 00:03:01.981
-[ Laughs ]
How about this?

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:17.029
-Okay, what you do is,
you be a real girlfriend.

00:03:17.029 --> 00:03:19.331
First of all,
when you're in a relationship,

00:03:19.331 --> 00:03:21.133
y'all supposed to
look out for each other.

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:22.968
Y'all supposed to have
each other's back.

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:25.004
You're not having his back
by letting him

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:28.140
going out and embarrassing
you and him in a damn crowd

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:30.609
with a terrible
Australian accent.

00:03:30.609 --> 00:03:32.812
So, when he starts
doing it, say, "Stop that!

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:34.514
That's not funny!
That's not funny!

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:36.849
Nobody likes that!
Nobody likes that!

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.117
Stop doing that!"

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:41.387
Then, if he doesn't stop --
if he doesn't stop,

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:45.992
you break up with him
and start dating an Australian.

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:47.627
-[ Laughs ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:53.399
-So every time now he see you,
you're with a real Australian.

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:54.600
-Uh-huh.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.603
-So he can hear what
the accent sounds like.

00:03:57.603 --> 00:04:00.372
-Yeah. And then point to your
boyfriend and you go,

00:04:00.372 --> 00:04:02.275
"You think this is funny?"

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:03.809
-Hey, you think
he's pulling it off?

00:04:03.809 --> 00:04:06.045
Is he pulling it off?

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:07.847
-Oh, my God.

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:09.815
-That is so stupid!
Why would you do that?!

00:04:09.815 --> 00:04:14.653
That's dumb!
-Okay.

00:04:14.653 --> 00:04:16.656
I can't wait to see you in
the next "Justice League."

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:18.123
I swear, I cannot wait.

00:04:18.123 --> 00:04:20.425
I cannot wait to see it.

00:04:20.425 --> 00:04:24.297
I just want to see the trailer.
Alright, here we go.

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:26.466
Oh, okay.

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:40.813
-Okay, I have two questions --
I have two answers for this.

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:42.648
'Cause this is
a sensitive thing.

00:04:42.648 --> 00:04:44.516
The first question
I would have to ask is,

00:04:44.516 --> 00:04:48.788
is she sure
she's not smelling herself?

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:50.223
Okay? First question.
-That's interesting.

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:54.626
-Okay, if it's the co-worker,
I'm very sensitive to this,

00:04:54.626 --> 00:04:57.262
Jimmy, because I used to be
an athlete.

00:04:57.262 --> 00:04:58.530
And I was a girl and, you know,

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:00.566
didn't really know
how to take care of myself.

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:03.068
So I didn't know to shave under
my arms and stuff like that.

00:05:03.068 --> 00:05:05.304
Sometimes, I'm musty.

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:09.575
You know, if you get musty,
and it's embarrassing.

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:11.076
-Yeah, musty.
-You know, it's embarrassing.

00:05:11.076 --> 00:05:13.713
So, what I would do is,
I would invite them into a room

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:15.014
and I would close the door.

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:19.085
And then the first thing I would
do is open up the window.

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:20.586
And I would let them see me
open up the window.

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:21.887
-Uh-huh.

00:05:21.887 --> 00:05:23.723
-And if they say, "Why are you
opening up the window?",

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:27.259
I would be like,
"Because you stink."

00:05:27.259 --> 00:05:31.631
And it's -- Because this is --
And let me tell you now,

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:34.333
that person's gonna appreciate
it, because all the [bleep]

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:37.870
that's been walking around
smelling him ain't said nothing.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.672
That's like letting somebody
be in front of you

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:41.307
with a booger in their nose
and you're not saying,

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:42.875
"Hey, get that booger."

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:45.644
-Yeah, it's kind of --
Well, some people agree,

00:05:45.644 --> 00:05:47.579
but, yeah, I think --

00:05:47.579 --> 00:05:49.848
-You've got to tell them.
You've gotta tell them, Jimmy.

00:05:49.848 --> 00:05:53.953
You've gotta tell them.
-But does it have to be me?

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:57.056
-Yes, because you're
the one that smells them.

00:05:57.056 --> 00:05:58.591
-Mm...

00:05:58.591 --> 00:05:59.692
-It's -- Wait a minute.

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:01.927
Oh, this is about
somebody you work with?

00:06:01.927 --> 00:06:04.730
-No! No! I mean, no.

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:06.498
-Oh, I was finna say,
bring them out right now

00:06:06.498 --> 00:06:07.533
so I can tell them.

00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:10.068
-No, no. Yeah.
[ Laughs ]

00:06:10.068 --> 00:06:11.637
That's why we're friends.

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:13.439
"Leslie,
you gotta do me a favor."

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:14.907
Yeah, yeah. No, no.
I don't know this person.

00:06:14.907 --> 00:06:16.342
No, this is a fan.

00:06:16.342 --> 00:06:19.144
But I just feel like, yeah,
if someone else can do that --

00:06:19.144 --> 00:06:20.646
I don't know.
It's like you just go, "Hey --"

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:22.648
-Nah. The person that smells it

00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:25.951
has got to be
the person that tells it.

00:06:25.951 --> 00:06:28.554
-Did you know that rhymed?

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:31.724
-No, I didn't.
[ Both laugh ]

00:06:31.724 --> 00:06:36.529
-Okay, here we go.
This one here is the last one.

00:06:42.268 --> 00:06:45.304
-Get another [bleep] roommate!
What?!

00:06:45.304 --> 00:06:47.407
No. What?!

00:06:47.407 --> 00:06:48.908
-That's why we ask you.
We love you.

00:06:48.908 --> 00:06:51.577
That is all the time we have
for "Life Coach."

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:52.945
My thanks to Leslie Jones.

